# Placeholder so the empty MacOS/ directory is tracked in git.
#
# This is the source-of-truth skeleton for /Applications/cmux Computer Use.app.
# It deliberately lives under `scripts/CmuxCuaBundle/` (NOT a
# `.app` suffix) so macOS LaunchServices on developer machines does
# not index it as a second installed app with the `com.cmuxterm.cua`
# bundle id. With the previous `scripts/cmux Computer Use.app/` shape, every
# `cargo run` from inside the repo would surface a "ghost CmuxCua"
# entry in System Settings → Privacy & Security pointing at the empty
# skeleton path.
#
# At build / install time the cmux-cua release binary (universal
# macOS slice — arm64 + x86_64 lipo'd together) is copied into this
# directory as `cmux-cua`. The Info.plist's CFBundleExecutable
# points at that name.
#
# See:
#   - .github/workflows/cd-rust-cmux-cua.yml  (copies the skeleton's
#     Contents/ into the release tarball at CD time and adds the
#     universal binary)
#   - libs/cmux-cua/scripts/install.sh        (downloads the
#     resulting tarball, extracts it to /Applications/cmux Computer Use.app,
#     and creates the ~/.local/bin/cmux-cua symlink pointing into
#     the bundle)
